// Cycle of Life: Realistic Fauna — FotSA cats (Pantherinae + Machairodontinae).
//
// Apex carnivores, auto-detected as predators via the "huntable" tag (they hunt every herbivore in
// range). Tuning here: slow apex lifecycles, very low predation vulnerability, a prey requirement
// that keeps them genuinely limited by the herbivore base, and DEN SUPPRESSION for the solitary
// cats — the den heuristic (predator + group spawn) gave every cat a family den, but only the social
// ones (lions, and the likely-social sabertooths) raise young communally. Solitary cats get
// "den": { "enabled": false }.
//
// preyPerPredator = standing prey units needed to sustain one cat; higher = more limited by prey.
// breedingMonths = birth months. K=1 already (these are deliberately rare).
//
// huntWhenFull = the fraction of the full kill rate a SATED cat keeps (0 = stops when full). Felids
// are documented surplus killers: a single leopard once killed 51 sheep in a pen, and snow leopards
// are notorious for slaughtering whole corrals of goats. Livestock-raiding spotted cats (leopard,
// snow leopard) get the strongest floor; the big social/solitary cats a modest opportunistic one;
// the sabertooths keep 0 — megafauna specialists whose huge kills feed them for days, no reason to
// keep killing.
{
  "species": {

    // ---- Lions: social prides — keep the den ----
    "pantherinae:pantherinae-panthera-leo-normal": {
      "predationVulnerability": 0.04, "preyPerPredator": 6, "growthRate": 0.1, "huntWhenFull": 0.15,
      "lifecycle": { "lifespanDays": 5400, "gestationDays": 110, "litterSizeMin": 1, "litterSizeMax": 4, "breedingMonths": [3, 4], "juvenileMortality": 0.5 }
